WEBVTT

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:04.550
From Start Here, choose Deploy a Cluster and select Foundation V M.

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:07.862
Use this method when you have the classic Foundation virtual machine

00:00:07.862 --> 00:00:08.400
service.

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:13.150
Foundation Central and standalone F C A are different backends.

00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:16.975
Review supported hardware and software for your environment.

00:00:17.388 --> 00:00:20.300
The guided journey opens existing workflows;

00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.312
moving between guidance stages does not deploy a cluster or mark it

00:00:24.312 --> 00:00:24.950
verified.

00:00:26.142 --> 00:00:28.567
Open Cluster Create for Foundation V M.

00:00:29.204 --> 00:00:33.192
Enter the actual Foundation endpoint and service port, not a Prism

00:00:33.204 --> 00:00:35.154
address or browser page path.

00:00:35.567 --> 00:00:37.804
Select the required credential references.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:41.967
Confirm that the appliance can reach Foundation and the provisioning

00:00:41.979 --> 00:00:42.604
networks.

00:00:43.004 --> 00:00:44.942
Keep secrets in the credential store.

00:00:45.317 --> 00:00:49.979
Import a reviewed saved configuration when one exists, then inspect

00:00:49.979 --> 00:00:53.017
its targets rather than assuming the filename is correct.

00:00:54.171 --> 00:00:59.058
Stage the approved A H V and A O S installation files

00:00:59.071 --> 00:01:02.983
on Foundation, then refresh image inventory in the workflow.

00:01:03.358 --> 00:01:08.558
Choose the exact available filenames and supply the A H V I

00:01:08.696 --> 00:01:11.396
S O checksum expected by Foundation.

00:01:11.796 --> 00:01:15.483
An image mounted somewhere else is not necessarily available to its

00:01:15.496 --> 00:01:16.133
installer.

00:01:16.521 --> 00:01:19.458
Review upload gates and capacity before staging.

00:01:19.871 --> 00:01:23.358
Resolve inventory or checksum errors before imaging.

00:01:24.533 --> 00:01:29.946
Review each node serial, block identity and position, host name, host

00:01:30.046 --> 00:01:32.883
address, controller address and management address.

00:01:33.283 --> 00:01:36.946
Select the appropriate node role and supported controller memory.

00:01:37.358 --> 00:01:42.108
Check per-node management credential references, subnet masks, gateways

00:01:42.308 --> 00:01:43.658
and V LAN settings.

00:01:44.046 --> 00:01:48.058
Re-foundation can overwrite existing installations.

00:01:48.446 --> 00:01:52.833
A valid form or selected hardware platform does not itself establish

00:01:52.833 --> 00:01:55.933
vendor compatibility or permission to erase a node.

00:01:57.088 --> 00:01:59.312
Save the configuration and run Dry Run.

00:01:59.712 --> 00:02:04.125
Review the native schema checks, selected images, connectivity and

00:02:04.125 --> 00:02:06.712
credential findings that the workflow provides.

00:02:07.162 --> 00:02:08.262
Fix every blocker.

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:12.262
Review the generated target list and obtain approval for the exact

00:02:12.262 --> 00:02:14.788
configuration where policy requires it.

00:02:15.175 --> 00:02:18.412
Enter the required deployment confirmation deliberately.

00:02:18.812 --> 00:02:23.050
Saving, importing and approving are separate from actually selecting

00:02:23.062 --> 00:02:23.925
Run Workflow.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:29.038
Submit once, then follow the linked job and Foundation session.

00:02:29.438 --> 00:02:33.688
Read phase and node progress, logs and actual target state.

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:38.438
A missing response or interrupted browser is not a reason to submit

00:02:38.450 --> 00:02:39.150
imaging again.

00:02:39.562 --> 00:02:43.850
After Foundation finishes, confirm cluster identity and membership.

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.675
Continue to reviewed post-configuration.

00:02:47.088 --> 00:02:52.438
When initial access needs a password and EULA bootstrap, use the supported

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:55.375
bootstrap sequence before the required health verification.
